1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
One stale memory can put a whole team out of sync.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:15,000
BrainBob gives each agent the context it can access: individual notes, team knowledge, and company decisions. Here’s Maya starting a fresh session.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:27,000
She asks for the approved Atlas deadline. NVIDIA models on Crusoe answer from saved context, while Bob retrieves the files beside the conversation.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Open the citation. There’s the original approval, its author, and its source. You can inspect the evidence behind the answer.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Now Maya changes a preference: three short bullets instead of three sentences. Save the correction, and Bob files the new version.

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The previous memory stays in history.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
A fresh session uses the correction immediately. BrainBob: shared memory you can see, inspect, and improve.
